# Subagent Council Loop (mandatory — NOT Gauntlet)

**Owner name:** **Subagent Council Loop**  
**NOT the same as:** Gauntlet loop, gauntlet-critic scoring, BAR, meta-critic manifest, “make gate green.”

Agents have repeatedly skipped this process. **Do not apply code fixes until the council passes.**

Full reference: `docs/qa/SUBAGENT_COUNCIL_LOOP.md`

---

## When this loop is required

- **Any implementation turn** that changes gameplay, planning paint, settle/commit, tiles, or combat behavior — unless the owner explicitly says “skip council this once.”
- **Planning recovery** per `docs/design/planning/PLANNING_ACTION_FIX_PLAN_2026-08-31.md` — every layer.

**Not required:** read-only Q&A, doc-only edits the owner pasted verbatim, git commits with zero logic change.

---

## The loop (repeat until pass)

```
1. PROPOSE  — agent writes the fix (what, why, files, bible/rule cites). Do NOT edit code yet.
2. COUNCIL  — launch exactly 3 subagents (rules-only critics). Parallel OK.
3. VERDICT  — all 3 PASS → step 4. Any FAIL → revise proposal, new council (step 2). Do not patch from critic homework.
4. APPLY    — implement the approved proposal only.
5. VERIFY   — run the matching automated suite; report PASS/FAIL.
```

---

## Council job (rules only)

Each critic answers **only:**

> Does this **proposal** violate any project rule? If yes: **which rule** (file/name) and **what pattern**?

### Critics MUST check

- `docs/design/planning/MOVE_PREVIEW_RULES.md` (wins on planning paint/commit)
- `.cursor/rules/global-systems-first.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/move-preview-intent-truth.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/action-range-latest-stand.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/no-bandaid-fixes.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/no-heavy-postprocess-safety.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/planning-hover-perf-mandatory.mdc` (when touching hover perf)
- `.cursor/rules/qa-fix-no-heuristics.mdc` (when fixing QA FAILs)

### Critics MUST NOT

| Forbidden | Why |
|-----------|-----|
| Gauntlet scores (0–100), BAR, “threshold 85” | That is **Gauntlet Loop** — different process |
| Regression matrices, “run full gate” lists | Verification is step 5, not council |
| “Fix isn’t complete yet” / architecture wishlists | Council = **rule violations on the proposal**, not scope creep |
| Re-propose the implementation | Only: PASS or FAIL + rule cite |
| `gauntlet-critic` subagent for scoring gameplay | Use **generalPurpose** or explicit rules-only prompt below |

### Council prompt template (copy for each of 3 critics)

```
Subagent Council — rules only (NOT gauntlet).

Proposal: [paste proposal]

Answer ONLY:
- PASS or FAIL
- If FAIL: list each rule violated (rule file + one sentence). No scores. No extra fixes. No regression plan.
```

---

## Agent obligations after council

- **PASS (3/3):** Apply proposal → run QA per `qa-after-gameplay-changes.mdc` → changelog notes `Council: 3/3 PASS`.
- **FAIL:** New proposal addressing **cited rules only** → new council. **Do not** apply partial fixes from failed round.
- **Never** claim “critics failed so we can’t ship” while shipping without a council pass on what was applied.

---

## Wins over

- Applying fixes first, critics after (backwards)
- Using `gauntlet-critic` as the council (wrong tool)
- Treating council FAIL as “implement critic suggestions” without a new proposal + council
- Structural grep PASS as “follows rules” without behavioral bible checks (see action fix plan)
